  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infectious disease response capability improvement project through the establishment of the Accra Medical Diagnosis Center in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By establishing a medical examination center equipped with low-cost, bench-top, and fully automated equipment that can be used in low-income partner countries with high infection mortality rates, a system that can operate without skilled molecular diagnostic experts can strengthen Ghana&apos;s medical and healthcare systems. Through this, there is a high possibility that diagnostic medical centers of the same system can be expanded not only to other regions in Ghana but also to other low-income countries in Africa. Currently, in the event of an outbreak of infection in Ghana, it is difficult for most ordinary people to undergo diagnostic tests, so the medical examination center proposed by the project can be a clue to Ghana&apos;s universal healthcare system in Ghana. In addition to creating employment in healthcare-related occupations, it is possible to generate revenue from the employment of various occupations in healthcare centers and the provision of various medical services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improvement of accessibility to diagnostic services for Ghanaian through the establishment of diagnostic center, Increasing incomes of local staffs by capacity building of medical diagnosis centers, Improving awareness for HPV and Antimicrobial resistance of Ghanaian&#xc758;&#xb8cc;&#xc9c4;&#xb2e8;&#xc13c;&#xd130; &#xc124;&#xb9bd;&#xc744; &#xd1b5;&#xd55c; &#xac00;&#xb098; &#xd604;&#xc9c0; &#xc8fc;&#xbbfc;&#xb4e4;&#xc758; &#xac10;&#xc5fc;&#xbcd1; &#xc9c4;&#xb2e8; &#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4; &#xc811;&#xadfc;&#xc131; &#xd5a5;&#xc0c1;, &#xc758;&#xb8cc;&#xc9c4;&#xb2e8;&#xc13c;&#xd130; &#xc778;&#xb825; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9;&#xac15;&#xd654;&#xb97c; &#xd1b5;&#xd55c; &#xc18c;&#xb4dd; &#xc99d;&#xb300;, &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed;&#xc8fc;&#xbbfc; HPV, &#xd56d;&#xc0dd;&#xc81c; &#xb0b4;&#xc131; &#xad00;&#xb828; &#xc778;&#xc2dd;&#xc99d;&#xc9c4;</narrative>
  </description>
